[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

Right-click the little alarm bell on the clock in the top right corner to open Set Alarm Time, without digging your watch out of your inventory. Left-click still turns the alarm on and off like vanilla.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Wear a digital watch, or hold an alarm clock.
[*]Right-click the bell to the right of the time. It's the same dialog the inventory's Set Alarm option opens, so OK saves the time and whether the alarm is on.
[*]Left-click the bell to toggle the alarm or stop it ringing, same as before.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Client side only. Can be added to an existing save.
[*]Analog watches have no alarm, so right-clicking their clock does nothing.
[*]Single player only. Split screen hasn't been tried.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Another mod's UI covering the top right corner can catch the right-click first, and the shortcut won't fire.
[*]If the click spot doesn't line up with the bell at your clock size (Options > Display), please report it with the size you use.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/clock-alarm-shortcut]GitHub[/url]
